From: Darrel Griet <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backports: Drop the trailing slash from BACKPORT_DIR

Every Kconfig of the integrated backports tree is pulled in as
source "$BACKPORT_DIR/.../Kconfig". With BACKPORT_DIR set to "backports/"
those expand with a double slash, e.g. backports//drivers/net/wireless/b43/
Kconfig. kconfig copes, but it records the names verbatim in
include/config/auto.conf.cmd, and in an out-of-tree build those
prerequisites are resolved through VPATH = $(srctree). GNU make's VPATH
search does not handle // inside a file name, so they are treated as
non-existent, include/config/auto.conf never becomes up to date, and make
restarts silentoldconfig forever without ever compiling anything.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [android vendor kernel]
---
--- a/backports/Kconfig
+++ b/backports/Kconfig
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 config BACKPORT_DIR
 	string
-	default "backports/"
+	default "backports"
 
 config BACKPORT_VERSION
 	string
